[N 29-30 Darnassus and Astranaar]
[D Forever Alliance 1-30 (Braedyn)\\Hand-in run at level 29: the Auberdine dock, Darnassus (Blackfathom, the fossil, Thundris), the Astranaar and Illiyana pickups, and an optional Stonetalon dip for the Gnomeregan quest chain.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel 29|r  -  you step off the Menethil boat onto the Auberdine dock at about level 29; hearth = Sentinel Hill and it stays there (chapter 22 hearths from it). This is a hand-in chapter with almost no killing: five turn-ins worth ~10,600 quest XP (Researching the Corruption, Bloom of the Heavens, Blackfathom Villainy, Twilight Falls, The Absent Minded Prospector), then pickups in Astranaar and at Illiyana's camp, then the optional Stonetalon dip. Level 30 is expected somewhere between here and the end of chapter 21
[OC]|cffffcc00Order:|r dock (Gershala, Thundris) > boat to Rut'theran Village and the portal up to Darnassus (Selgorm, Manados, Mathiel, Greywhisker) > flight to Astranaar > Illiyana's camp > optional Stonetalon dip > back to Astranaar. The Blackfathom quests (1275, 1199, 1200) and the Prospector's fossil (741) all clear here

[OC]|cffffffffAuberdine dock|r
At [TAR8997 Gershala Nightwhisper], [QT1275] (2,400 XP, the 8 brain stems from Blackfathom) [G38.3,43.0 Darkshore]
[OC]|cffffcc00Gear (1275):|r |cff66ff66Staghide Armguards|r (leather bracers +3 Agi +3 Sta) for both of you; a shaman who already wears Bands of Serra'kis (+6 Str +3 Sta) keeps them. Beetle Clasps are mail and the Prelacy Cape is a healer's cloak - pass
At [TAR3649 Thundris Windweaver], [QT98209] (1,200 XP, the Nord'el you carried from Sylessa in Menethil; no reward is listed in the DB. Wowhead lists this quest without Human, so a Human hunter will not hold it - skip the line) [G37.4,40.1 Darkshore]
|cFFfff8a3Board the boat to Rut'theran Village|r (about 5 minutes; if it has just left, flight master Caylais Moonfeather also flies there - you took that flight path in chapter 11) [G38.3,43 Darkshore]
[OC]On arrival walk into the portal in the village: it leads up to Darnassus

[OC]|cffffffffDarnassus|r  -  the portal arrives west of the bank (Classic-era spot 30,41, unverified on Forever). Route: north-east to Selgorm and Manados, south to Mathiel, the far south-west for Greywhisker, then back to the portal. No fighting anywhere in the city
At [TAR4783 Dawnwatcher Selgorm], [QT1200] (3,300 XP, the Head of Kelris) [G56.2,24.4 Darnassus]
[OC]|cffffcc00Gear (1200):|r Gravestone Scepter is a wand and Arctic Buckler a shield - neither of you can use either: vendor whichever you pick
At [TAR4784 Argent Guard Manados], [QT1199] (2,550 XP, the 10 Twilight Pendants; both rewards are fixed) [G55.2,24.0 Darnassus]
[OC]|cffffcc00Gear (1199):|r Heartwood Girdle (leather belt +5 Sta, +6 spell damage) is worth wearing only if your belt is bare - Moss Cinch from Aku'mai beats it. Nimbus Boots are cloth: vendor
[O][A Hunter] Level 30 already? At [TAR4146 Jocaste], [T] train your level 30 spells (Jocaste is in the far north, about 20 map units from Selgorm and Manados) [G40.4,8.6 Darnassus]
[OC][A Shaman] Darnassus has no shaman trainer: level 30 waits for Ironforge (chapter 24)
At [TAR6142 Mathiel], [QA2925 Klockmort's Essentials] (a 245-XP breadcrumb to Klockmort Spannerspan in Ironforge; it opens Essential Artificials, 3,050 XP, which is a Gnomeregan quest - chapter 24) [G59.5,45.4 Darnassus]
[O][A Hunter] Bow users: [TAR4173 Landria], the Bow Merchant, is the Darnassus arrow stop on the way south (her stock is not in the DB, so check for the level-25 Razor Arrow) [G63.3,66.3 Darnassus]
At [TAR2912 Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker] in the south-west corner, [QT741] [QA942 The Absent Minded Prospector] (the fossil goes on to Archaeologist Flagongut in Menethil Harbor, chapter 22. 741 is a level-20 quest, so it pays only 10-20 percent of its 1,150 XP at your level - the gloves are the point) [G31.2,84.5 Darnassus]
[OC]|cffffcc00Gear (741):|r |cff66ff66Hammerfist Gloves|r (leather +3 Str +3 Agi) for both of you, unless you wear the Naga Battle Gloves from Blackfathom. Windfelt Gloves are a caster pair (+3 Int, +4 spell damage) and the Relic Hunter Belt is cloth - pass
[OC]|cffffcc00Not for now:|r two more hand-ins live in Darnassus that this guide never routes back to. Thyn'tel Bladeweaver (61.8,39.2) takes Answered Questions (1044, 3,050 XP), the last step of the long Howling Vale chain through the Barrens, Stranglethorn and Darkshire, and Treshala Fallowbrook (69.5,67.8) takes Mortality Wanes (1142, 3,050 XP) from Razorfen Kraul. Skip both unless you hold the quest and want a second trip
Walk back to the portal to Rut'theran Village, west of the bank (Classic-era spot, unverified) [G30,41 Darnassus]
At flight master [TAR3838 Vesprystus], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Astranaar]|r (the game routes it through Auberdine - stay on the bird; if the map offers only Auberdine, fly there and take the Astranaar bird from Caylais Moonfeather) [G58.4,94 Teldrassil]

[OC]|cffffffffAstranaar|r  -  you land at the north tip of the island town; Llana and Faldreas stand a few steps south
[A Shaman] Use the Unfilled Blue Waterskin on the lake at the north tip of town, beside the flight master [UI265772 Unfilled Blue Waterskin] [QC94500] [G34.4,48.0 Ashenvale]
[OC][A Shaman] |cff66ff66Normal|r - one click. The quest says "the waters of Astranaar" and the skin's text says the body of water around the town; Classic-era sources put Astranaar on an island in a lake, so any shore works (the DB gives no exact spot). The Full Blue Waterskin goes back to Hervdana Saegrund in Wetlands with the Call of Water chain in chapter 22 - keep it
At [TAR3691 Raene Wolfrunner], [QA1024 Raene's Cleansing] (part 3 of the chain chapter 12 started - to Shael'dryn in the east, chapter 21) [G36.5,49.5 Ashenvale]
At [TAR3845 Shindrell Swiftfire], [QA4581 Kayneth Stillwind] (590-XP note to Kayneth Stillwind at Forest Song, chapter 21) [G34.7,48.8 Ashenvale]
At [TAR3894 Pelturas Whitemoon], [QA1035 Fallen Sky Lake] (3,050 XP; the Fallen Moonstone drops from the level-30 Shadethicket Oracle at 66.7,82.2 - chapter 21) [G36.9,51.5 Ashenvale]
At [TAR3970 Llana], [QA95737 Seeking Caitlin] (a 630-XP breadcrumb to Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor; it opens the Excavation Site chain, chapter 22) [G35.0,48.5 Ashenvale]
[O]At [TAR3996 Faldreas Goeth'Shael], [QA1056 Journey to Stonetalon Peak] (a level-18 breadcrumb, about 70 XP now; take it only if you will do the Stonetalon dip below) [G35.8,49.1 Ashenvale]

[OC]|cffffffffWest: Illiyana's camp|r  -  15 map units west along the road; chapter 21's satyr chain ends here
At [TAR3901 Illiyana], [QA1021 Vile Satyr! Dryads in Danger!] (a 2,550-XP breadcrumb to Anilia at Xavian in the east; chapter 21 hands it in and continues with The Branch of Cenarius) [G21.7,53.3 Ashenvale]
[O]At [TAR3880 Sentinel Melyria Frostshadow], [QA1022 The Howling Vale] (2,450 XP at level 30 for a single click on a tome - see the note below) [G22.2,53.0 Ashenvale]
[OC]|cffffcc00The Howling Vale:|r the Tome of Mel'Thandris lies at about 50.5,39.1 (cave mouth near 53,37.6), 8 map units north of Shael'dryn's moonwell. Click it (|cff66ff66normal|r, apart from that rare) when chapter 21's east loop reaches Shael'dryn, and hand in to Melyria when that chapter brings you back to Illiyana's camp. Another guide warns that a rare roams the cave: pull carefully. Melyria then offers Velinde Starsong (1037, 610 XP), the first step of a long chain through the Barrens and Stranglethorn: decline it
[OC]If you skip the Stonetalon dip, walk east back to Astranaar now: everything in the next block is optional

[OC]|cffffffffStonetalon dip (optional)|r  -  about 20 minutes. It gives you Castpipe's Task (2931, 230 XP), which unlocks Data Rescue (3,650 XP) in the Gnomeregan chapter, plus Stonetalon Peak's flight path and a few hundred XP of old breadcrumbs. Skip it and Data Rescue stays locked
[OC]|cffffcc00Alonso|r the Knight Errant (43,70) stands a few steps from the cave mouth (42.3,71.0) and offers three Dragonslayer quests (2,550 XP each, no objective text in the DB). Chapter 12 skipped them. Take one only if you already hold its item: the Lance (bought from a Dark Iron Entrepreneur in Dun Modr, chapter 19) or the Shield (looted behind Gath'Ilzogg in Stonewatch Keep, chapter 16's side note). Season of Discovery mechanics, unverified on Forever: accept and hand in on the same visit. The Helm is behind Commander Springvale in Shadowfang Keep - skip it
[O]At [TAR210995 Alonso], [QA78134 Dragonslayer's Lance] [QT78134] (only with the Lance in your bags) [G43.0,70.1 Ashenvale]
[O]At [TAR210995 Alonso], [QA78133 Dragonslayer's Shield] [QT78133] (only with the Shield in your bags) [G43.0,70.1 Ashenvale]
[O]Run through the cave into Stonetalon Mountains [G42.3,71.0 Ashenvale]
[O]At [TAR4080 Kaela Shadowspear], [QT1070] [QA1085 On Guard in Stonetalon] (830 + 165 XP, both level-21 quests: only 200-400 XP at your level) [G59.9,66.8 Stonetalon Mountains]
[O]At [TAR4077 Gaxim Rustfizzle], [QT1085] [QA2931 Castpipe's Task] (its other follow-up, A Gnome's Respite, is Venture Co. kills at level 18-20, grey at your level: decline it) [G59.5,67.2 Stonetalon Mountains]
